module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf.PowerTransitionDescent

/-!
# The transitions collapse the identification across degrees

Let `S` be a scheme, `𝒜` a graded `𝒪_S`-algebra (Situation 01NN) and `T` a test scheme. The
union `F(T)` of the display 01NX is the set of quadruples of positive degree modulo two
identifications: strict equivalence inside a degree, and the equivalence of Tag 01NW across
degrees. The transitions `F_d(T) → F_{a d}(T)` of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf.Fd.scale` are maps the first identification is
already compatible with.

This file proves that the **second** identification is *generated by the transitions*: two
quadruples compatible at a common multiple `m = a d = a' d'` of their degrees become **strictly
equivalent** — not merely equivalent — once both are transported to the degree `m`. So two
classes of `F_d(T)` and `F_{d'}(T)` that the union identifies are already the same class of
`F_{d d'}(T)`, which is the sense in which `F(T)` is the colimit of the `F_d(T)` along the
transitions rather than just a set receiving compatible maps from them.

## Why this is the content of the first step of Tag 01NY

The Stacks proof of Tag 01NY builds the scheme representing `F` as the union of the schemes
`U_d` representing the `F_d` along the morphisms `U_d → U_{d'}` that the transitions
`F_d → F_{d'}` correspond to. For that union to represent `F` rather than something larger, a
point of `F(T)` must be a point of some `F_d(T)` *and* two points of `F_d(T)`, `F_{d'}(T)` must
be identified in `F(T)` only when the transitions already identify them. The first is the
construction of `F(T)` as a union; the second is the theorem below.

## The comparison

A compatibility of `(d, f, L, ψ)` with `(d', f, L', ψ')` at `(a, a')` is, by
`...Quadruple.CompatibleAt`, a family of isomorphisms
`γ_{p, q} : L^{⊗ p} ≅ (L')^{⊗ q}` indexed by the common multiples `(p, q) = (n a, n a')` of
`(a, a')`, multiplicative and compatible with `ψ`. A strict equivalence of the two transitions
`(m, f, L^{⊗ a}, ψ^{(a)})` and `(m, f, (L')^{⊗ a'}, (ψ')^{(a')})` is an isomorphism of the
Laurent algebras of `L^{⊗ a}` and `(L')^{⊗ a'}` carrying `ψ^{(a)}` to `(ψ')^{(a')}`. The two are
the same data read twice: the degree-`i` component of the comparison is the component `γ_{i a,
i a'}` of the family conjugated by the power-of-a-power comparisons of
`...powPowIso` on both sides,

`(L^{⊗ a})^{⊗ i} ≅ L^{⊗ (i a)} ≅ (L')^{⊗ (i a')} ≅ ((L')^{⊗ a'})^{⊗ i}`,

and the multiplicativity of the conjugated family is the multiplicativity of `γ` conjugated by
the two instances of `...powPowIso_mul`. The only genuine bookkeeping is that the two
transitions have the degrees `a d` and `a' d'`, which are equal but not identical, so one of them
has to be read at the other's spelling; that is `...Quadruple.congrDegree`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf.Twisting.congrDegree` and
  `...Quadruple.congrDegree`: a quadruple of degree `d` read as one of degree `e`, for `d = e`,
  and `...Fd.congrDegree` the induced bijection `F_d(T) → F_e(T)`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf.scalePairIso`: **the isomorphism of the Laurent
  algebras of `L^{⊗ a}` and `(L')^{⊗ a'}` induced by a comparison of two quadruples at
  `(a, a')`.**

## Main results

* `...RelativeProjQcohSheaf.Quadruple.strictlyEquivalent_scale_of_compatibleAt`: **two
  quadruples compatible at `(a, a')` have strictly equivalent transitions to the common
  multiple `a d = a' d'` of their degrees.**
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf.Quadruple.strictlyEquivalent_scale_of_equivalent`
  and `...Fd.scale_eq_of_equivalent`: **equivalent quadruples of positive degrees `d` and `d'`
  have the same class in `F_{d d'}(T)` after the transitions**, so the identification across
  degrees that the union of the display 01NX makes is generated by the transitions.

## What is not here

Representability is not proved and nothing is assumed: there is no scheme anywhere below. The
two further steps of Tag 01NY that this does not take are recorded on
`...Fd.scale_eq_of_equivalent`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Section 01NS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NY)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory MonoidalCategory

open AlgebraicGeometry Stacks.RingedSpace Stacks.PullbackTensorCoherence
open Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorPower

attribute [local instance] Stacks.PullbackGradedAlgebra.monoidalCategory

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf

open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf.LaurentPullback

attribute [local instance] isInvertible_piece

variable {T S : Scheme.{u}} {f : T ⟶ S}
  {A : SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.{u, u} (structureRingSheaf S.toRingedSpace)} {d d' : ℤ}

/-! ### Reading a quadruple at another spelling of its degree -/

namespace Twisting

variable {L : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureRingSheaf T.toRingedSpace)}
  [Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible T.toRingedSpace.presheaf (isSheafStruct T) L]

/-- **The map `ψ` of a quadruple of degree `d` read as the map of a quadruple of degree `e`**,
for `e` another spelling of `d`: the degree-`i` component is the component of `ψ` in that degree,
with its source `f^*𝒜_{i e}` transported to `f^*𝒜_{i d}`.

Both degrees are equal, so this is a transport and no mathematics; it is needed because the
transition to a common multiple `m = a d = a' d'` of two degrees produces quadruples over
`a d` and over `a' d'`, which are the same integer written two ways. -/
def congrDegree (ψ : Twisting f A d L) {e : ℤ} (h : d = e) : Twisting f A e L where
  app i := (pullbackFunctor (ringedSpaceHom f)).map
      (eqToHom (congrArg A.piece (show i * e = i * d by rw [h]))) ≫ ψ.app i
  app_mul i j := by
    subst h
    simpa using ψ.app_mul i j
  app_one := by
    subst h
    simpa using ψ.app_one

/-- The components of the reread map are the components of `ψ`, with the degree transported. -/
@[simp] theorem congrDegree_app (ψ : Twisting f A d L) {e : ℤ} (h : d = e) (i : ℤ) :
    (ψ.congrDegree h).app i =
      (pullbackFunctor (ringedSpaceHom f)).map
          (eqToHom (congrArg A.piece (show i * e = i * d by rw [h]))) ≫ ψ.app i :=
  rfl

end Twisting

namespace Quadruple

/-- **A quadruple of degree `d` read as a quadruple of degree `e`**, for `e` another spelling of
`d`. The invertible module is unchanged and the map `ψ` is `Twisting.congrDegree`. -/
def congrDegree (P : Quadruple f A d) {e : ℤ} (h : d = e) : Quadruple f A e where
  L := P.L
  isInvertible := P.isInvertible
  twisting := P.twisting.congrDegree h
  epi_app_one := by
    subst h
    have := P.epi_app_one
    change Epi ((pullbackFunctor (ringedSpaceHom f)).map
      (eqToHom (congrArg A.piece (show 1 * d = 1 * d from rfl))) ≫ P.twisting.app 1)
    infer_instance

/-- The invertible module of a reread quadruple is unchanged. -/
@[simp] theorem congrDegree_L (P : Quadruple f A d) {e : ℤ} (h : d = e) :
    (P.congrDegree h).L = P.L :=
  rfl

/-- The components of the map `ψ` of a reread quadruple. -/
@[simp] theorem congrDegree_twisting_app (P : Quadruple f A d) {e : ℤ} (h : d = e) (i : ℤ) :
    (P.congrDegree h).twisting.app i =
      (pullbackFunctor (ringedSpaceHom f)).map
          (eqToHom (congrArg A.piece (show i * e = i * d by rw [h]))) ≫ P.twisting.app i :=
  rfl

/-- **Rereading the degree respects strict equivalence.** -/
theorem StrictlyEquivalent.congrDegree {P Q : Quadruple f A d} (hPQ : StrictlyEquivalent P Q)
    {e : ℤ} (h : d = e) :
    StrictlyEquivalent (P.congrDegree h) (Q.congrDegree h) := by
  subst h
  obtain ⟨β, γ, h1, hψ⟩ := hPQ
  refine ⟨β, γ, h1, fun n => ?_⟩
  change (pullbackFunctor (ringedSpaceHom f)).map
      (eqToHom (congrArg A.piece (show n * d = n * d from rfl))) ≫
        P.twisting.app n ≫ γ.hom.app n = _
  rw [hψ n]
  rfl

end Quadruple

/-- **The bijection `F_d(T) → F_e(T)` of two spellings of one degree.** -/
def Fd.congrDegree {A : SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.{u, u} (structureRingSheaf S.toRingedSpace)}
    {d e : ℤ} (h : d = e) (ξ : Fd A d T) : Fd A e T :=
  ⟨ξ.1,
    Quotient.map (sa := Quadruple.setoid ξ.1 A d) (sb := Quadruple.setoid ξ.1 A e)
      (fun P => P.congrDegree h) (fun _ _ hPQ => hPQ.congrDegree h) ξ.2⟩

/-- Rereading the degree sends the class of a quadruple to the class of the reread quadruple. -/
@[simp] theorem Fd.congrDegree_mk
    {A : SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.{u, u} (structureRingSheaf S.toRingedSpace)} {d e : ℤ}
    (h : d = e) (f : T ⟶ S) (P : Quadruple f A d) :
    Fd.congrDegree h (Fd.mk f P) = Fd.mk f (P.congrDegree h) :=
  rfl

/-! ### Inverting a multiplicativity square -/

/-- **A multiplicativity square with isomorphisms for its vertical maps can be inverted.** -/
private theorem inv_mul_square {C : Type*} [Category C] [MonoidalCategory C]
    {A₁ A₂ A₃ B₁ B₂ B₃ : C} (e₁ : A₁ ≅ B₁) (e₂ : A₂ ≅ B₂) (e₃ : A₃ ≅ B₃)
    (m : A₁ ⊗ A₂ ⟶ A₃) (m' : B₁ ⊗ B₂ ⟶ B₃)
    (h : m ≫ e₃.hom = (e₁.hom ⊗ₘ e₂.hom) ≫ m') :
    m' ≫ e₃.inv = (e₁.inv ⊗ₘ e₂.inv) ≫ m := by
  have hee : (e₁.inv ⊗ₘ e₂.inv) ≫ (e₁.hom ⊗ₘ e₂.hom) = CategoryStruct.id (B₁ ⊗ B₂) :=
    (MonoidalCategory.tensorIso e₁ e₂).inv_hom_id
  rw [← Category.id_comp (m' ≫ e₃.inv), ← hee, Category.assoc,
    ← Category.assoc (e₁.hom ⊗ₘ e₂.hom), ← h, Category.assoc, e₃.hom_inv_id, Category.comp_id]

/-! ### The comparison induced on the Laurent algebras of the two powers -/

section ScalePair

variable {L L' : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureRingSheaf T.toRingedSpace)}
  [Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible T.toRingedSpace.presheaf (isSheafStruct T) L]
  [Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible T.toRingedSpace.presheaf (isSheafStruct T) L']
  {a a' : ℤ}

/-- The family of comparisons a compatibility of two quadruples at `(a, a')` consists of: an
isomorphism `L^{⊗ p} ≅ (L')^{⊗ q}` for every common multiple `(p, q)` of `(a, a')`. -/
abbrev ScaledFamily (L L' : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureRingSheaf T.toRingedSpace))
    [Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible T.toRingedSpace.presheaf (isSheafStruct T) L]
    [Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible T.toRingedSpace.presheaf (isSheafStruct T) L']
    (a a' : ℤ) :=
  ∀ p q : ℤ, Quadruple.IsScaledPair a a' p q → ((laurent L).piece p ≅ (laurent L').piece q)

/-- The multiplicativity of such a family, as `...Quadruple.CompatibleAt` asserts it. -/
abbrev IsMulScaledFamily (γ : ScaledFamily L L' a a') : Prop :=
  ∀ (p q p' q' : ℤ) (h : Quadruple.IsScaledPair a a' p q)
      (h' : Quadruple.IsScaledPair a a' p' q'),
    MonoidalCategoryStruct.tensorHom (γ p q h).hom (γ p' q' h').hom ≫
        (laurent L').mulSheaf q q' =
      (laurent L).mulSheaf p p' ≫ (γ (p + p') (q + q') (h.add h')).hom

/-- The component of the family at the common multiple `(i a, i a')` of `(a, a')`. -/
abbrev familyAt (γ : ScaledFamily L L' a a') (i : ℤ) :
    (laurent L).piece (i * a) ≅ (laurent L').piece (i * a') :=
  γ (i * a) (i * a') ⟨i, rfl, rfl⟩

/-- **The family is compatible with reindexing both degrees.** The two components are the same
morphism: the indexing is by equalities of integers, and those are proof-irrelevant. -/
theorem familyAt_reindex (γ : ScaledFamily L L' a a') {p q p₁ q₁ : ℤ} (hp : p = p₁)
    (hq : q = q₁) (h : Quadruple.IsScaledPair a a' p q)
    (h₁ : Quadruple.IsScaledPair a a' p₁ q₁) :
    (reindexIso L hp).hom ≫ (γ p₁ q₁ h₁).hom = (γ p q h).hom ≫ (reindexIso L' hq).hom := by
  subst hp
  subst hq
  change CategoryStruct.id _ ≫ _ = _ ≫ CategoryStruct.id _
  rw [Category.id_comp, Category.comp_id]

/-- **The family is multiplicative with its total degrees prescribed**, in the bidegree
`(i a, j a)` with total degrees `((i + j) a, (i + j) a')`: the multiplicativity of the family
followed by `familyAt_reindex`, which moves it across the identification of `i a + j a` with
`(i + j) a`. -/
theorem mulPairIso_familyAt (γ : ScaledFamily L L' a a') (hmul : IsMulScaledFamily γ)
    (i j : ℤ) :
    (mulPairIso L (degMul (rfl : i + j = i + j) a)).hom ≫ (familyAt γ (i + j)).hom =
      ((familyAt γ i).hom ⊗ₘ (familyAt γ j).hom) ≫
        (mulPairIso L' (degMul (rfl : i + j = i + j) a')).hom := by
  have hγ := hmul (i * a) (i * a') (j * a) (j * a') ⟨i, rfl, rfl⟩ ⟨j, rfl, rfl⟩
  rw [mulSheaf_laurent, mulSheaf_laurent] at hγ
  have hre := familyAt_reindex γ (degMul (rfl : i + j = i + j) a)
    (degMul (rfl : i + j = i + j) a')
    (show Quadruple.IsScaledPair a a' (i * a + j * a) (i * a' + j * a') from
      ⟨i + j, by ring, by ring⟩)
    ⟨i + j, rfl, rfl⟩
  change ((mulIso L (i * a) (j * a)).hom ≫
      (reindexIso L (degMul (rfl : i + j = i + j) a)).hom) ≫ (familyAt γ (i + j)).hom =
    ((familyAt γ i).hom ⊗ₘ (familyAt γ j).hom) ≫ ((mulIso L' (i * a') (j * a')).hom ≫
      (reindexIso L' (degMul (rfl : i + j = i + j) a')).hom)
  rw [Category.assoc, hre]
  have hγ' := congrArg
    (fun z => z ≫ (reindexIso L' (degMul (rfl : i + j = i + j) a')).hom) hγ
  simp only [Category.assoc] at hγ' ⊢
  exact hγ'.symm

/-- **The degreewise comparison `(L^{⊗ a})^{⊗ i} ⟶ ((L')^{⊗ a'})^{⊗ i}` induced by a comparison
of two quadruples at `(a, a')`**: the power-of-a-power comparison read backwards, the component
of the family at `(i a, i a')`, and the power-of-a-power comparison on the `L'` side. -/
def scalePairApp (γ : ScaledFamily L L' a a') (i : ℤ) :
    (laurent (powModule L a)).piece i ⟶ (laurent (powModule L' a')).piece i :=
  (powPowIso L a i).inv ≫ (familyAt γ i).hom ≫ (powPowIso L' a' i).hom

/-- The degreewise comparison in the other direction, built from the inverses. -/
def scalePairInvApp (γ : ScaledFamily L L' a a') (i : ℤ) :
    (laurent (powModule L' a')).piece i ⟶ (laurent (powModule L a)).piece i :=
  (powPowIso L' a' i).inv ≫ (familyAt γ i).inv ≫ (powPowIso L a i).hom

/-- **The power-of-a-power comparisons carry the family to the induced comparison**: the square
that the whole construction exists to make commute, and which holds by definition. -/
theorem powPowIso_scalePairApp (γ : ScaledFamily L L' a a') (i : ℤ) :
    (powPowIso L a i).hom ≫ scalePairApp γ i =
      (familyAt γ i).hom ≫ (powPowIso L' a' i).hom := by
  rw [scalePairApp]
  exact (powPowIso L a i).hom_inv_id_assoc _

/-- **The induced degreewise comparison is multiplicative in every integral bidegree**, which is
the `map_mul` law of a homomorphism of sheaves of graded algebras. The two instances of
`...powPowIso_mul`, for `L` with `a` and for `L'` with `a'`, identify the multiplications of the
two Laurent algebras of the powers with those of the Laurent algebras of `L` and `L'` in the
bidegrees `(i a, j a)` and `(i a', j a')`, and there the multiplicativity is the one the family
has. -/
theorem scalePairApp_mulSheaf (γ : ScaledFamily L L' a a') (hmul : IsMulScaledFamily γ)
    (i j : ℤ) :
    SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.mulSheaf (laurent (powModule L a)) i j ≫
        scalePairApp γ (i + j) =
      (scalePairApp γ i ⊗ₘ scalePairApp γ j) ≫
        SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.mulSheaf (laurent (powModule L' a')) i j :=
  conj_mul_square (powPowIso L a i) (powPowIso L a j) (powPowIso L a (i + j))
    (powPowIso L' a' i) (powPowIso L' a' j) (powPowIso L' a' (i + j)) _ _ _ _
    (familyAt γ i).hom (familyAt γ j).hom (familyAt γ (i + j)).hom
    (powPowIso_mul L a i j) (powPowIso_mul L' a' i j) (mulPairIso_familyAt γ hmul i j)

/-- **The comparison in the other direction is multiplicative too**, by inverting the square of
`mulPairIso_familyAt` and conjugating it the other way round. -/
theorem scalePairInvApp_mulSheaf (γ : ScaledFamily L L' a a') (hmul : IsMulScaledFamily γ)
    (i j : ℤ) :
    SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.mulSheaf (laurent (powModule L' a')) i j ≫
        scalePairInvApp γ (i + j) =
      (scalePairInvApp γ i ⊗ₘ scalePairInvApp γ j) ≫
        SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.mulSheaf (laurent (powModule L a)) i j :=
  conj_mul_square (powPowIso L' a' i) (powPowIso L' a' j) (powPowIso L' a' (i + j))
    (powPowIso L a i) (powPowIso L a j) (powPowIso L a (i + j)) _ _ _ _
    (familyAt γ i).inv (familyAt γ j).inv (familyAt γ (i + j)).inv
    (powPowIso_mul L' a' i j) (powPowIso_mul L a i j)
    (inv_mul_square (familyAt γ i) (familyAt γ j) (familyAt γ (i + j)) _ _
      (mulPairIso_familyAt γ hmul i j))

/-- **The isomorphism of the Laurent algebras of `L^{⊗ a}` and `(L')^{⊗ a'}` induced by a
comparison of two quadruples at `(a, a')`.** The two directions are the conjugates of the two
directions of the family, and they are mutually inverse degreewise because the conjugating
power-of-a-power comparisons cancel. -/
def scalePairIso (γ : ScaledFamily L L' a a') (hmul : IsMulScaledFamily γ) :
    laurent (powModule L a) ≅ laurent (powModule L' a') where
  hom := homOfMulSheaf _ _ (scalePairApp γ) (scalePairApp_mulSheaf γ hmul)
  inv := homOfMulSheaf _ _ (scalePairInvApp γ) (scalePairInvApp_mulSheaf γ hmul)
  hom_inv_id := SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.Hom.ext fun i => by
    change scalePairApp γ i ≫ scalePairInvApp γ i =
      CategoryStruct.id ((laurent (powModule L a)).piece i)
    simp only [scalePairApp, scalePairInvApp, Category.assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc,
      Iso.inv_hom_id]
  inv_hom_id := SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.Hom.ext fun i => by
    change scalePairInvApp γ i ≫ scalePairApp γ i =
      CategoryStruct.id ((laurent (powModule L' a')).piece i)
    simp only [scalePairApp, scalePairInvApp, Category.assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc,
      Iso.inv_hom_id_assoc, Iso.inv_hom_id]

/-- The degree-`i` component of `scalePairIso γ hmul` is `scalePairApp γ i`. -/
@[simp] theorem scalePairIso_hom_app (γ : ScaledFamily L L' a a') (hmul : IsMulScaledFamily γ)
    (i : ℤ) : (scalePairIso γ hmul).hom.app i = scalePairApp γ i :=
  rfl

end ScalePair

/-! ### The transitions to a common multiple are strictly equivalent -/

namespace Quadruple

variable {P : Quadruple f A d} {Q : Quadruple f A d'}

/-- **Two quadruples compatible at a common multiple of their degrees have strictly equivalent
transitions to that multiple.** This is the theorem the file exists for: the identification
across degrees made by the union of the display 01NX is already made by the transitions
`F_d → F_{a d}`, inside the single degree `m = a d = a' d'`.

The witness is `scalePairIso`, the comparison of the compatibility conjugated by the
power-of-a-power comparisons on both sides. Its compatibility with `ψ` is the compatibility of
the family: the transition of `ψ` to the degree `a d` is `ψ` in the degree `i a` followed by the
power-of-a-power comparison, and that comparison cancels against the copy inside `scalePairIso`,
leaving exactly the clause the family satisfies in the degrees `(i a, i a')`. -/
theorem strictlyEquivalent_scale_of_compatibleAt {a a' : ℤ} (ha : 0 < a) (ha' : 0 < a')
    (h : CompatibleAt P Q a a') (hm : a' * d' = a * d) :
    StrictlyEquivalent (P.scale ha) ((Q.scale ha').congrDegree hm) := by
  obtain ⟨hm0, γ, hmul, _, hψ⟩ := h
  refine (strictlyEquivalent_iff_exists_hom _ _).mpr ⟨scalePairIso γ hmul, fun i => ?_⟩
  change P.twisting.scaleApp a i ≫ scalePairApp γ i =
    (pullbackFunctor (ringedSpaceHom f)).map
        (eqToHom (congrArg A.piece (show i * (a * d) = i * (a' * d') by rw [hm]))) ≫
      Q.twisting.scaleApp a' i
  have hfam := hψ (i * a) (i * a') ⟨i, rfl, rfl⟩
  simp only [Twisting.scaleApp, scalePairApp, Category.assoc, Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc]
  rw [← Category.assoc (P.twisting.app (i * a)), hfam]
  simp [← Functor.map_comp_assoc]

/-- **Equivalent quadruples of positive degrees `d` and `d'` have strictly equivalent transitions
to the degree `d d'`.** Equivalence is compatibility at `(d', d)`, so this is the theorem above at
that pair. -/
theorem strictlyEquivalent_scale_of_equivalent (hd : 0 < d) (hd' : 0 < d') (h : Equivalent P Q) :
    StrictlyEquivalent (P.scale hd') ((Q.scale hd).congrDegree (mul_comm d d')) :=
  strictlyEquivalent_scale_of_compatibleAt hd' hd h (mul_comm d d')

end Quadruple

/-- **The identification across degrees made by the union of the display 01NX is generated by
the transitions.** Two equivalent quadruples of positive degrees `d` and `d'` — which the union
`F(T)` identifies, by `...F.mk_eq_mk_of_equivalent` — already have the *same class in
`F_{d d'}(T)`* after the transitions `F_d(T) → F_{d d'}(T)` and `F_{d'}(T) → F_{d d'}(T)`.

Together with `...Fd.toF_scale`, which says the canonical maps `F_d(T) → F(T)` identify a class
